From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ai-blaise <engineering@blaise.tech>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Report citus.* USERSET GUCs to clients

FEATURE: T2

Citus exposes many USERSET GUCs whose values affect query planning and
execution (router fast-path, local-execution, propagate_set_commands,
shard_count, etc.). When a session-pooler such as ai-blaise/citus-pool
multiplexes client backends across PostgreSQL backends, the pool can
only preserve transaction-pooling semantics if it observes SET commands
for those GUCs through ParameterStatus (S) packets.

Without GUC_REPORT, a SET citus.enable_router_execution = off on one
client session is invisible to the pool layer, so a subsequent client
attached to the same backend can inherit the wrong planner mode.

Extend the existing OverridePostgresConfigProperties() loop -- which
already toggles GUC_REPORT for search_path -- to mark every citus.*
USERSET GUC with GUC_REPORT. PGC_INTERNAL and superuser-only contexts
retain their default flags because they cannot be reset by a regular
session.

This is a one-place, upstream-PR-friendly change: it does not modify
the individual DefineCustom* call sites, so the patch is a small diff
to a single helper function. The upstream-PR draft is tracked in
docs/ai-blaise/UPSTREAM_SYNC.md.
---
 src/backend/distributed/shared_library_init.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/backend/distributed/shared_library_init.c b/src/backend/distributed/shared_library_init.c
index 646151be5..f1a25d7bc 100644
--- a/src/backend/distributed/shared_library_init.c
+++ b/src/backend/distributed/shared_library_init.c
@@ -3000,6 +3000,22 @@ OverridePostgresConfigProperties(void)
 		{
 			var->flags |= GUC_REPORT;
 		}
+
+		/*
+		 * FEATURE: T2
+		 *
+		 * Mark every citus.* USERSET GUC with GUC_REPORT so a session pooler
+		 * in front of Citus can observe SET commands via the PostgreSQL
+		 * ParameterStatus (S) protocol packet. Without this, transaction-
+		 * pooling routers cannot preserve planner-affecting GUC state across
+		 * multiplexed client sessions and may execute a follow-up client's
+		 * query under stale router or execution settings.
+		 */
+		if (var->context == PGC_USERSET &&
+			strncmp(var->name, "citus.", strlen("citus.")) == 0)
+		{
+			var->flags |= GUC_REPORT;
+		}
 	}
 }
 
